  "vibe": "An affinage cave held at 11°C: cave brown (#3c3630) ground, golden rind (#d9a441), pale paste (#f4e8c8) and red wax (#8c3a2e) for the sharp edges. Bree Serif gives titles a pressed-slab weight; Sarala keeps the ledgers legible. Behind the type, two shelf planks carry six cheese wheels drawn as stacked ellipses — some gold, some cream, one cut open to wax red — while humidity droplets fall down the left and a wax-red hygrometer column rises and falls on sin(0.6t) beside typeset readings of 11°C and 94% RH. A vast 60px ink ellipse arches over the top like a cellar mouth. Statements flip to full wax red; the CTA lands on gold. It owns a drag-and-drop turning day, a dial cave control, a board of wheel ages and a fade morph.",
